Choplifter! PCjr -- M10 polish
hardware validation (workset bytes, /ztimer)  ground BROWN

BIOS model byte at F000:FFFE ... FD (IBM PCjr)
int 12h 640 KB, pages on entry CRT=7 CPU=7
  JrConfig: not found
  no JrConfig /V window -- using pages 6 and 7 (the /V64 pair).
  On jrIDE, load DEVICE=JRCONFIG.SYS /V64 /L instead of forcing DOS pages.
  video pages A=6 B=7
stick 1 x=35 y=35 live; btn=0; INT15 x=128 y=128 ok
axes port 201h; deadzone +/-16/255 around 128; joystick 1 = bits 0,1
Plug joystick 1 (first connector).  Centre, then SPACE on the
title.  C opens calibrate.  Up = thrust, down = descend,
left/right = tilt and translate.  Ctrl-A / Ctrl-V invert X / Y.
Esc on the title quits to DOS.

Flew with blit_rle_m8 + SN76496 + M9 presentation (M10 polish) on pages 6/7.  Sim 20 Hz (every 3 retraces).  Controls: Keyboard.  Stick source this run: keys only.
Measured: 583 sim ticks / 1746 retraces in 1300 BIOS ticks = 8.16 Hz sim (target 20.00).

